nDepartment of Biology Graduate\nbio\nAbout\nClimate and Diversity\nOur Department\nGreen Team\nFacilities\nBusiness Office\nFrequently Asked Questions\nLocation and Maps\nContact Us\nLife in Central PA\nGraduate\nProgram Requirements\nProgram Options\nFinancial Support\nHow to Apply\nContact the Department\nBiology GSA\nStudent Awards\nTravel Funds Request Form\nBiology Graduate Student Handbook\nUndergraduate\nUndergraduate Portal\nAdvising\nAcademic Programs\nResearch\nProspective Students\nAfter Graduation\nBecoming a Learning Assistant or Laboratory Teaching Assistant\nGlobal Opportunities\nStudent Engagement\nStudent Resources\nBiology Syllabi\nPeople\nNews\nEvents\nResearch\nBiology Greenhouse\nAlumni/Giving\nGiving to Biology\ngrad\nProgram Requirements\nProgram Options\nMolecular Evolutionary Biology Option\nFinancial Support\nHow to Apply\nContact the Department\nBiology GSA\nStudent Awards\nTravel Funds Request Form\nBiology Graduate Student Handbook\nMake advancements in science and in your academic journey.\nPenn State\u2019s Department of Biology is one of the top-ranked biology departments in the United States. Students in the graduate program can pursue both M.S. and Ph.D. degrees in many areas of biology, including cell and developmental biology, genetics, genomics, physiology, neurobiology, organismal biology, plant science, ecology, evolutionary biology, and theoretical and computational biology.\nProgram Requirements\nProgram Options\nFinancial Support\nContact Us\nProgram Admissions\nAdmission to our program is based on merit as presented in your application and evaluated by the faculty, available space in a particular program, and the availability of financial support. Year-round assistantships and fellowships are guaranteed for five years to all biology graduate students (in good academic standing). We will be accepting applications on a rolling review basis through December 10.\nHow to Apply\nStudent Resources\nThe Graduate School\nGraduate E